From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: BetterVR's ImGui overlay starts on the first Options
 press and draws a stage A panel, behind bettervr.json's menu switch

The Linux backend had no overlay (vulkan_imgui.cpp was Win32 only). With bettervr.json's "menu" at 1,
Options on the right Sense (bound to the mod menu action in the Touch profile, in place of the left X) opens and
closes the menu on a short press. The overlay is made on the first open, on Cemu's recording thread, with one
text font, its own render target and no help images. Its font atlas goes up with the backend's own submit and
queue wait under ps5xr::QueueMutex, on Cemu's queue, as the one PS5 graphics queue is shared. The panel is drawn
into the overlay's target and blitted to the HUD quad in place of Cemu's HUD image, which is only read. Every
phase logs one [menu] init line, and a failed init closes the menu for good. With the switch at 0 nothing of it
runs; the mod menu stays shut as patch 0008 left it.
